    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="18.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 18.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="18.2" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="300" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ ure<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_18-2.lnote.oe.1"/> ælc oðrum beode þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> we willon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_18-2.lnote.oe.2"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man us beode: þ<hi rend="italic">æt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_18-2.lnote.oe.3"/></hi> is rihtlic dóm ⁊ Gode<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_18-2.lnote.oe.4"/> swiðe gecweme; ⁊ se byð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_18-2.lnote.oe.5"/> swiðe gesælig, þe þone dom gehylt.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="18.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="300" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ ure ælc oðru<hi rend="italic">m</hi> beode þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> we wyllan, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man us beode: þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> is rihtlic dóm ⁊ Gode swiðe gecwéme; ⁊ se bið swiðe gesæli, ðe ðæne dóm gehealt.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="18.2" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="300" ed="#liebermann"/>And ælc ure oðrum beode þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> we wyllan, þæt man us beode: þ[<hi rend="italic">æt</hi>]<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_18-2.lnote.oe.1-3"/> is rihtlic dom ⁊ Gode swyþe gecweme; ⁊ se byð swiðe sælig, þe þonne dom gehealt.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="18.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="301" ed="#liebermann"/>Et quod nobis fieri uolumus, aliis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_18-2.lnote.oe.1-2"/> faciamus: hoc iudicium iustum est; et sane beatus et Deo gratus est, qui iudicium hoc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_18-2.lnote.oe.2-2"/> sincere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_18-2.lnote.oe.3-2"/> tenuerit ad gloriam omnipotentis Dei, cuius sumus miseratione conditi et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_18-2.lnote.oe.4-2"/> pretio magno redempti.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="18.2" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="301" ed="#liebermann"/>Faciamusque unusquisque alii quod sibi uellet ab eo fieri: hoc est iustum iudicium et Deo acceptissimum; felix qui hoc iudicium obseruauerit,</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="18b.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="168" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ ure ælc oðrum beode þæt we wyllan þæt man us beode; þæt is<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#ICn_18-2.robnote.fn.11"/> rihtlic dóm ⁊ Gode swiðe gecwéme; ⁊ se bið swiðe gesæli<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#ICn_18-2.robnote.fn.12"/> ðe ðæne dóm gehealt.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="248" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And ure ælc oðrum beode þæt we willon þæt man us beode; þæt is rihtlic dom and Gode swiðe gecweme; and se byð swiðe gesælig þe þone dom gehylt.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="301" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_18-2.lnote.de.1"/> jeder<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_18-2.lnote.de.2"/> von uns erzeige dem andern, was wir wollen, dass uns erzeigt werde; das ist ein gerechter und Gott höchst wohlgefälliger Grundsatz<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_18-2.lnote.de.3"/>; und der wird höchst selig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_18-2.lnote.de.4"/> sein, wer solchen Grundsatz festhält.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_18-2.lnote.de.5"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let each of us offer the other what we wish to be offered to us: that is a just principle and most pleasing to God; and he will be most blessed who keeps that principle.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_18-2.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="169" ed="#robertson"/>And each of us shall treat others as we desire ourselves to be treated; that is a just maxim and very pleasing to God; and he who upholds that maxim shall be greatly blessed.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="249" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And let each of us treat others as we wish to be treated; that is a just rule and most pleasing to God; and the person who adheres to that rule will be very happy.</ab>
        <note type="passageSource">cf. Matt. 7:12; Ps. 105:3</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="301"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_49">VI Atr 49</ref>; Psalm 105, 3</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. VI Atr. 49 | (*Vgl. Psalm 105, 3)</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="357"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_49">VI Atr 49</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 18:2: VI Atr 49</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VI Atr 49.; Robertson (p. 139) takes I Cn from B, which begins at ‘mæssedæg’ in 14.2, the earlier clauses being supplied from G; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 301, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">þæt is: þis A</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_18-2.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">300</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æ. u. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æ. u. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_18-2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">300</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-lan <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-lan Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_18-2.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">300</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þis is rihtlice <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þis is rihtlice Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_18-2.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">300</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">God <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">God Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_18-2.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">300</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">biþ s. sælig þe þoñe d. gehealt <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">biþ s. sælig þe þoñe d. gehealt Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_18-2.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">301</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">alii <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">alii K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_18-2.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">301</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_18-2.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">301</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">t. s. <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">t. s. K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_18-2.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">301</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Dm K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Dm K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_18-2.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">300</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þis <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> þ. is</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þis instead of þ. is</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_18-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">18, 3. 18, 2, also umgeordnet, bringt <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 144; fast ganz steht 18, 2 dort p. 282; ganz 37. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Moral 2. 4f., Gerechtigkeit 3f.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">18, 3. 18, 2, thus rearranged, appear in <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 144; 18, 2 stands there almost in full on p. 282, and in full on 37. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Moral 2. 4f., Gerechtigkeit 3f.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_18-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">So rühmen den Satz viele Homileten; <hi rend="italic">s. o</hi>. zu VI Atr 49⁵</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Many homilists praise the saying in these terms; <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> on VI Atr 49⁵</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_18-2.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht ‘Urteil’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not ‘judgement’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_18-2.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">201</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Beati qui custodiunt iudicium et faciunt iustitiam</hi>; Ps. 105, 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Beati qui custodiunt iudicium et faciunt iustitiam</hi>; Ps. 105, 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_18-2.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">201</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht ‘Urteil sprach’; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Wb healdan</hi> 11. Jene Hom. 282 sagt: <hi rend="italic">þe þæne dom gehealdeð, geearnað him sylfum</hi> Lohn im Himmel</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not ‘pronounced judgement’; <hi rend="italic">cf. Wb healdan</hi> 11. That Hom. 282 says: <hi rend="italic">þe þæne dom gehealdeð, geearnað him sylfum</hi> reward in heaven</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_18-2.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">350</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. VI Atr. 49; Wulfstan, pp. 37, 144, 282.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_18-2.robnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">168</biblScope></bibl><label>is</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">þis</hi> A instead of <hi rend="italic">ꝥ. is.</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_18-2.robnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">168</biblScope></bibl><label>gesæli</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">(<hi rend="italic">ge</hi>)<hi rend="italic">sælig</hi> G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
